 and target location"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_012ShbeZSDLy31XtcanvD9sw","tool_input":{"command":"/Users/auderyliu/Documents/NTU/project/agentic-pbt-main/envs/lxml-html-clean/bin/python -c \"import lxml_html_clean.clean as c, hypothesis, lxml; print(c.__file__, lxml.__version__)\"","description":"Locate target module in venv"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_018u6rt1DtiMAhLKqZ3KTLC4","tool_input":{"command":"sed -e 's/out = clean_html(html)$/out = clean_html(\"<div>\" + html + \"<\\/div>\")/' -e 's/out = Cleaner(safe_attrs_only=False).clean_html(html)/out = Cleaner(safe_attrs_only=False).clean_html(\"<div>\" + html + \"<\\/div>\")/' test_clean_pbt.py > test_clean_pbt_wrapped.py && grep -n 'clean_html(' test_clean_pbt_wrapped.py && python -m pytest -q test_clean_pbt_wrapped.py 2>&1 | grep -E \"Failing|html=|Error|passed|failed|assert\" | head -40","timeout":600000,"description":"Run wrapped variant of property tests"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":23,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I found one real bug in `lxml_html_clean.clean`: it crashes on some short, realistic HTML fragments.\n\n**What fails:**\n```python\nfrom lxml_html_clean import clean_html\nclean_html('<button><script>alert(1)</script></button>')   # AssertionError\n```\n`'<button><iframe></iframe></button>'` fails the same way. With `Cleaner(safe_attrs_only=False)`, so does `'<select><iframe></iframe></select>'`.\n\n- **Severity:** Medium, crash type.\n- **When it happens:** the fragment's outermost element is a tag the cleaner deletes along with its contents (e.g. `<button>`, `<textarea>`), and something inside it is also queued for removal.\n- **Cause:** the cleaner can't delete the outermost element, so it turns it into an empty `<div>` (`clean.py:443-449`). That detaches its children, but they stay in the removal queues. The cleanup loop then calls `drop_tree()`/`drop_tag()` on elements with no parent, and lxml's `assert parent is not None` fires. `<button><b>x</b></button>` doesn't crash because nothing inside it is queued.\n- **Impact:** any app that runs untrusted input through `clean_html` can be made to throw an unhandled exception. Running Python with `-O` turns it into an `AttributeError`, but it still crashes.\n- **Fix:** add `_kill.clear(); _remove.clear()` right after `el.clear()`. I applied it at runtime (monkeypatch, source file unchanged) and all three failing inputs then return `'<div></div>'`.\n\n**What passed:** I also checked that cleaned output, parsed again with lxml, never contains:\n- dangerous tags (`script`, `iframe`, `form`, `meta`, ...);\n- `on*` attributes;\n- `javascript:`/`vbscript:`/`data:text` URLs, including encoded or whitespace-split variants;\n- `expression(`, `@import` or `javascript:` inside `<style>`.\n\nThat held over 7,000 generated inputs (wrapped in `<div>` to avoid the crash), across default cleaning, cleaning twice, and `safe_attrs_only=False`. This only checks lxml's own parser, not how a real browser would parse the output: html5lib isn't installed.\n\n**Not reported:** `<base href=\"http://evil.com/\">` survives cleaning. A `<base>` tag changes where every relative link on the page points, so this could be a security concern. But the docs never say `<base>` is removed, so I left it out of the report.\n\nThree of the six tests in `test_clean_pbt.py` still fail, on purpose: they're the unwrapped versions that hit the crash.\n\nFiles are in `runs/lxml-html-clean/`:\n- `bug_report_lxml_html_clean_clean_2026-10-05_21-03_4f8j.md`\n- `test_clean_pbt.py`","ttft_ms":2269,"type":"result","d